# Enumeration data for the first nonsplit Held model

The 384 rows are permutations on the published sixteen-point carrier. A row
stores sixteen base-16 digits, in increasing order of the input point. The
inverse tables are checked by kernel reduction. The transition table packs four
nine-bit indices for right multiplication by A, B, A⁻¹ and B⁻¹; its meaning and
exhaustiveness are proved in `Enumeration`.

Rows are ordered by breadth-first search in A and B. `parent` and `lastGen`
record a shorter generator word for each noninitial row. External enumeration
only supplies these data: every property used by the proof is checked in Lean.

Source problem: Huppert--Blackburn III, XII.1.18(b), p.314, citing Held,
J. Algebra 8 (1968), 436--449, DOI 10.1016/0021-8693(68)90054-9.
-/

